  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-vision-toolkit",
      "text": "Vision toolkit for DeepSeek Harness -- give text-only agents the ability to see images."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it does",
      "text": "Provides CLI tools that call a vision API (DeepSeek VL, GPT-4V, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint) to describe, locate, detect, and crop elements from images. Registered as a dsh skill so agents know when and how to use them."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "- `glance` -- describe, ask about, or OCR an image\n- `ground` -- locate a specific element (returns bounding box)\n- `detect` -- find all instances of an element kind\n- `crop` -- cut a region from an image"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile your-profile add dsh-plugin-vision-toolkit\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Set environment variables:\n\n```bash\nexport VISION_API_KEY=sk-xxx           # Vision API key (falls back to DEEPSEEK_API_KEY)\nexport VISION_BASE_URL=https://...     # API endpoint (falls back to DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL)\nexport VISION_MODEL=deepseek-vl2       # Vision model name\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage examples",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Describe an image",
      "text": "glance screenshot.png"
    },
    {
      "section": "Ask a question",
      "text": "glance screenshot.png -q \"What error is shown?\""
    },
    {
      "section": "OCR",
      "text": "glance screenshot.png --ocr"
    },
    {
      "section": "Find a button",
      "text": "ground screenshot.png \"the login button\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Find all buttons",
      "text": "detect screenshot.png \"buttons\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Crop a region",
      "text": "crop screenshot.png 450,820,620,870 button.png\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "The plugin registers a skill in the system prompt that teaches the agent about the vision tools. When the agent encounters an image (user pastes one, references a screenshot, etc.), it calls the appropriate CLI tool which:\n\n1. Reads the image file\n2. Encodes it as base64\n3. Sends it to the vision API with a prompt\n4. Returns the text response\n\nThe agent never sees raw pixels -- it gets text descriptions it can reason about."
    },
    {
      "section": "Supported vision providers",
      "text": "- DeepSeek VL (deepseek-vl2, deepseek-vl2.5)\n- OpenAI GPT-4V / GPT-4o\n- Any OpenAI-compatible multimodal endpoint"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT -- YYTbit"
    }
